of the Earth now for 70 years.

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:00.520
We're here.

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:05.283
We've had genocides, Holocausts,
we've had the black plague,

00:22:05.283 --> 00:22:08.500
we've had world wars, we're here.

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:09.333
And everyone--

00:22:09.333 --> 00:22:10.250
- The human spirit is resilient.

00:22:10.250 --> 00:22:13.760
- It's unstoppable and
everybody's dwelling right now

00:22:13.760 --> 00:22:17.232
on a rise of nationalism
and hate which is terrible.

00:22:17.232 --> 00:22:19.660
However, let's contextualize it.

00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:24.660
And, instead of judging people
and calling them racists

00:22:25.110 --> 00:22:29.000
or bad people, why don't
you go loud about good?

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:31.820
Instead of getting sucked
in to being doing more hate

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:34.780
around people who hate, why
don't you actually combat it.

00:22:34.780 --> 00:22:37.970
Why don't we learn from Martin Luther King

00:22:37.970 --> 00:22:40.130
and from Gandhi and from
other people in the past.

00:22:40.130 --> 00:22:44.220
Which is you do not defeat
hate with hate on hate.

00:22:44.220 --> 00:22:46.710
You defeat hate with love at scale.

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:50.690
And we all have our 14
followers, our 1,000 followers,

00:22:50.690 --> 00:22:54.050
our eight followers and instead of flexing

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:56.974
about your new handbag
or your hot new sneakers

00:22:56.974 --> 00:23:01.974
or the hike you took or the
remarkable meal you're having,

00:23:02.120 --> 00:23:04.650
what about putting out good,
what about cosigning somebody

00:23:04.650 --> 00:23:06.270
that did something nice?

00:23:06.270 --> 00:23:09.500
What about watching somebody
open a door for an old lady

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:11.790
and roll up on them and make a video

00:23:11.790 --> 00:23:14.350
and tell them about this nice kid.

00:23:14.350 --> 00:23:17.750
We need to get louder about happiness.

00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:19.400
If we all collectively do that,

00:23:19.400 --> 00:23:20.840
I have a funny feeling the internet

00:23:20.840 --> 00:23:22.190
will feel a lot more happy.

00:23:22.190 --> 00:23:23.514
- Yeah, I mean that's what this is.

00:23:23.514 --> 00:23:25.860
There's a little quote book
it's called "Seize the Yay"

00:23:25.860 --> 00:23:28.270
like the podcast it's a
happy quote for every day.

00:23:28.270 --> 00:23:29.103
- I love that.

00:23:29.103 --> 00:23:30.840
- And people like
everywhere just I'm like,

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:34.400
life is pretty awesome, we're
in a really exciting time.

00:23:34.400 --> 00:23:36.641
It's a great time to be
alive, be excited about it.

00:23:36.641 --> 00:23:38.780
- 400 trillion to one.

00:23:38.780 --> 00:23:39.800
- Yeah.

00:23:39.800 --> 00:23:43.110
- 400 trillion to one, that
is the current scientific odds

00:23:43.110 --> 00:23:44.742
around being a human being.

00:23:44.742 --> 00:23:46.158
- And that's something that a--

00:23:46.158 --> 00:23:48.200
- Did you know that, 400 trillion to one.

00:23:48.200 --> 00:23:49.870
You were more likely to get struck

00:23:49.870 --> 00:23:52.660
by lightning ten times in
your life than have one.

00:23:52.660 --> 00:23:54.310
It is the great miracle.

00:23:54.310 --> 00:23:57.170
Like that whole miracle concept,
like the baby's a miracle!

00:23:57.170 --> 00:23:58.394
It's actually true.

00:23:58.394 --> 00:24:02.270
It's actually true and so
people are walking around moping

00:24:02.270 --> 00:24:06.640
about their mom being
a jerk or their brother

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:08.730
stealing their money or somebody, I mean--

00:24:08.730 --> 00:24:10.030
- Or their pimple on their face.

00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:11.520
- Or their pimple on their face

00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:14.410
or they can't get a new supreme.

00:24:14.410 --> 00:24:15.420
I mean, just or--

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:18.320
- The Gary Vee sneaker sold
out, it was like so fucked up.

00:24:19.360 --> 00:24:20.920
- Or like stuff that, I don't know

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:23.150
why this specific thing drives me crazy.

00:24:23.150 --> 00:24:26.180
People yelling at baristas
for using the wrong milk.

00:24:26.180 --> 00:24:29.540
I mean that to me, I don't
know what it is about that one.

00:24:29.540 --> 00:24:31.377
You know, people literally
yelling at somebody,

00:24:31.377 --> 00:24:33.220
"No almond milk, you asshole!"

00:24:33.220 --> 00:24:34.630
They just bought a $6 coffee,

00:24:34.630 --> 00:24:36.163
do you know how blessed you are?

00:24:36.163 --> 00:24:36.996
- (laughing) Yeah.

00:24:36.996 --> 00:24:39.610
I mean, a $9 coffee, Gary, come on.

00:24:39.610 --> 00:24:40.563
- Respect.

00:24:40.563 --> 00:24:41.640
(laughing)

00:24:41.640 --> 00:24:42.723
- So just to wrap up quickly.

00:24:42.723 --> 00:24:43.556
- Yes.

00:24:43.556 --> 00:24:45.350
- I want to give a little shout out

00:24:45.350 --> 00:24:47.640
to one of our mutual friends Justin Dry

00:24:47.640 --> 00:24:49.572
and the incredible work
that he's doing with Vino.

00:24:49.572 --> 00:24:50.405
- Yes.

00:24:50.405 --> 00:24:51.238
- Vinomofo.
- Yes.

00:24:51.238 --> 00:24:54.160
- You are here to launch
Empathy Wines in Australia.

00:24:54.160 --> 00:24:54.993
- Yes.

00:24:54.993 --> 00:24:56.420
- Which is so, so exciting.

00:24:56.420 --> 00:24:58.010
So just quickly give
us a run down on that.

00:24:58.010 --> 00:24:59.870
- So I started a winery almost

00:24:59.870 --> 00:25:01.900
a year ago called Empathy Wines.

00:25:01.900 --> 00:25:04.179
The ambition is to produce
and incredible wine

00:25:04.179 --> 00:25:07.540
in U.S. dollars, a $40 wine for 20 bucks.

00:25:07.540 --> 00:25:10.075
Obviously there's some price
variations here in Australia.

00:25:10.075 --> 00:25:12.620
Justin and I have been
friendly for a long time.

00:25:12.620 --> 00:25:14.830
We only wanted to sell direct to consumer

00:25:14.830 --> 00:25:17.160
from winery to people in America.

00:25:17.160 --> 00:25:19.540
He reached out, we got
into a conversation.

00:25:19.540 --> 00:25:21.880
There's such warm feelings
there and admiration.

00:25:21.880 --> 00:25:25.373
We got into a convo and Vinomofo
is the exclusive partner

00:25:25.373 --> 00:25:28.400
of being able to sell
the wine outside the U.S.

00:25:28.400 --> 00:25:31.153
in the Australia, New
Zealand, and Singapore market.

00:25:32.010 --> 00:25:36.289
And the response has been
remarkable in this marketplace.

00:25:36.289 --> 00:25:37.458
- It's a beautiful rosé.

00:25:37.458 --> 00:25:38.291
- Thank you.

00:25:38.291 --> 00:25:39.124
- Californian grapes.

00:25:39.124 --> 00:25:40.610
- And the white just came out and the red

00:25:40.610 --> 00:25:41.700
will be coming out in the fall

00:25:41.700 --> 00:25:46.270
and so it's been incredible
project and it's really.

00:25:46.270 --> 00:25:49.170
You know, it's funny, when
I was making the rosé,

00:25:49.170 --> 00:25:51.700
I was thinking about an Australian rosé.

00:25:51.700 --> 00:25:53.390
There's an Australian
rosé that I'm very fond of

00:25:53.390 --> 00:25:56.330
called Turkey Flat and I remember

00:25:56.330 --> 00:25:58.340
as I was blending it,
the whole time I'm like,

00:25:58.340 --> 00:26:00.190
I'm gonna make a better
rosé than Turkey Flat.

00:26:00.190 --> 00:26:01.980
I'm gonna make a better rosé
than and Whispering Angel.

00:26:01.980 --> 00:26:03.780
Those were the two things
I was thinking about.

00:26:03.780 --> 00:26:07.000
And so, it's been a lot
of fun and the partnership

00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:10.220
with Vinomofo has been extremely seamless

00:26:10.220 --> 00:26:12.690
and completely built on
kindness and friendship

00:26:12.690 --> 00:26:16.460
and empathy and I'm enjoying it.

00:26:16.460 --> 00:26:18.540
- So exciting to see it go live tonight!

00:26:18.540 --> 00:26:19.373
- Thank you, thank you.

00:26:19.373 --> 00:26:20.206
- So excited, we'll be partying.

00:26:20.206 --> 00:26:21.860
So two last questions.

00:26:21.860 --> 00:26:23.320
- Yes.

00:26:23.320 --> 00:26:25.040
- What are the three most
interesting things about you

00:26:25.040 --> 00:26:26.871
that don't normally
come up in conversation

00:26:26.871 --> 00:26:28.570
and you are probably the
hardest guest to come up

00:26:28.570 --> 00:26:30.900
with anything that hasn't
been on a podcast before.

00:26:30.900 --> 00:26:33.950
- I'm remarkable non
confrontational in real life,

00:26:33.950 --> 00:26:36.074
even though I'm a tough
guy on video and stage.

00:26:36.074 --> 00:26:37.193
- Nice.

00:26:39.160 --> 00:26:40.848
- I sleep seven to eight hours a day.

00:26:40.848 --> 00:26:41.681
- No.

00:26:41.681 --> 00:26:43.210
- Yep, yep.

00:26:43.210 --> 00:26:44.043
- Amazing.

00:26:44.043 --> 00:26:45.008
- I mean six and five when I travel.

00:26:45.008 --> 00:26:47.072
- It's possible!

00:26:47.072 --> 00:26:48.033
- And.

00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:52.780
I really don't, I genuinely don't care

00:26:52.780 --> 00:26:54.660
if I'm financially successful.

00:26:54.660 --> 00:26:56.400
Like, deeply.

00:26:56.400 --> 00:26:59.430
Like almost to the point
where I have to be careful

00:26:59.430 --> 00:27:01.800
'cause I almost can feel as I'm evolving

00:27:01.800 --> 00:27:03.994
the want to sabotage myself.

00:27:03.994 --> 00:27:04.990
(laughing)

00:27:04.990 --> 00:27:07.500
I'm not kidding, I like
really have to be thoughtful.

00:27:07.500 --> 00:27:10.640
I'm really having a very
interesting time with myself

00:27:10.640 --> 00:27:14.670
where I'm like, man I really almost like

00:27:14.670 --> 00:27:16.760
and I've said it a lot
which means it's like

00:27:16.760 --> 00:27:18.670
I get into this weird
like am I gonna become

00:27:18.670 --> 00:27:20.481
like a weird monk and just disappear?

00:27:20.481 --> 00:27:21.570
I'm.

00:27:21.570 --> 00:27:22.560
- Am I gonna go like.

00:27:22.560 --> 00:27:24.393
- I'm just all about happiness.

00:27:25.290 --> 00:27:27.400
And maybe my version of a weird monk

00:27:27.400 --> 00:27:31.550
is actually to just become a
junk and baseball card dealer.

00:27:31.550 --> 00:27:33.870
Right, like just really go there.

00:27:33.870 --> 00:27:35.490
But I can feel it in me.

00:27:35.490 --> 00:27:37.600
- You gonna Marie Kondo yourself.

00:27:37.600 --> 00:27:38.433
- Maybe.

00:27:38.433 --> 00:27:39.266
- That's next.

00:27:39.266 --> 00:27:40.099
- Maybe, I'm just a very.

00:27:42.170 --> 00:27:43.732
Things are very clear to me.

00:27:43.732 --> 00:27:44.565
- I like that.

00:27:44.565 --> 00:27:45.398
- And they have nothing to do

00:27:45.398 --> 00:27:47.070
with the modern version of success.

00:27:47.070 --> 00:27:48.703
This is not about stuff.

00:27:49.550 --> 00:27:52.920
This is about waking up
and not having anxiety.

00:27:52.920 --> 00:27:53.940
- I love that.

00:27:53.940 --> 00:27:55.260
And final question to finish up.

00:27:55.260 --> 00:27:56.257
- Yep.

00:27:56.257 --> 00:27:58.320
- What's your favorite motivational quote?

00:27:58.320 --> 00:27:59.220
- I don't know.

00:27:59.220 --> 00:28:01.200
- It can be a Gary Vee
quote, that's also fine.

00:28:01.200 --> 00:28:02.340
You can make it up on the spot.

00:28:02.340 --> 00:28:04.528
- I will and I can tell
you like what I think about

00:28:04.528 --> 00:28:08.960
which is kindness is karma, right?

00:28:08.960 --> 00:28:12.720
Give more than you take and
probably wrapping it up,

00:28:12.720 --> 00:28:14.490
probably my favorite thing to say

00:28:14.490 --> 00:28:16.180
'cause it hits people once in a blue moon,

00:28:16.180 --> 00:28:18.580
doing the right thing is
always the right thing.

